# Search Component Usage

## Intent
The global search (Cmd+K) provides quick navigation and actions. When adding new pages or actions to the application, they should be registered in the search configuration so users can discover and access them.

## When to Update Search

Add to search when:
- Creating a new navigable page in the application
- Adding a new user action (logout, toggle theme, etc.)
- Adding features users might want to access quickly

Skip search registration for:
- API routes
- Internal components without direct user access
- Pages already covered by parent routes

## File Location

Search configuration is in `apps/web/hooks/use-search-results.ts`

## Adding a New Page

1. Add the page path to `apps/web/constants/pages.ts` if not already present
2. Add an entry to `PAGES_CONFIG` array:

```ts
{
  id: "unique-page-id",
  label: "Page Display Name",
  icon: RiIconName,
  keywords: ["search", "terms"],
  description: "Brief description",
},
```

3. Add the path mapping to `PAGE_PATHS`:

```ts
"unique-page-id": PAGES.SECTION.PAGE_NAME,
```

4. Import the icon from `@repo/ui/icon`

### Example: Adding a Reports Page

```ts
// In PAGES_CONFIG
{
  id: "reports",
  label: "Reports",
  icon: RiFileChartLine,
  keywords: ["analytics", "stats", "data"],
  description: "View reports and analytics",
},

// In PAGE_PATHS
reports: PAGES.APPLICATION.REPORTS,
```

## Adding a New Action

Actions execute functions instead of navigating. Add to the `actions` array inside `useSearchResults`:

```ts
{
  id: "action-id",
  label: "Action Name",
  icon: RiIconName,
  keywords: ["search", "terms"],
  description: "What this action does",
  handler: () => {
    // Action logic here
  },
},
```

### Example: Adding a Copy Link Action

```ts
{
  id: "copy-link",
  label: "Copy Link",
  icon: RiLinkLine,
  keywords: ["share", "url", "clipboard"],
  description: "Copy current page URL",
  handler: () => {
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(window.location.href);
  },
},
```

## Role-Based Pages

For pages that require specific roles (admin, owner, etc.), add a comment noting the requirement. The filtering logic can be extended by passing user context to `performSearch`:

```ts
// Admin-only page
{
  id: "admin-settings",
  label: "Admin Settings",
  icon: RiAdminLine,
  keywords: ["admin"],
  description: "System administration", // Requires admin role
},
```

## Checklist

- [ ] Page path added to `apps/web/constants/pages.ts`
- [ ] Entry added to `PAGES_CONFIG` with id, label, icon, keywords, description
- [ ] Path mapping added to `PAGE_PATHS`
- [ ] Icon imported from `@repo/ui/icon`
- [ ] Run `pnpm checks` to validate

## Examples

### ✅ Good
Adding a new Settings sub-page and registering it in search with relevant keywords so users can find it by typing "notifications" or "alerts".

### ❌ Bad
Creating a new dashboard widget page but not adding it to search, making it only accessible via sidebar navigation.
